Phasmid: WebGL strings, limits, precision and extensions

What:     Every WebGL1 and WebGL2 context reports gpu.webgl or gpu.webgl2:
          UNMASKED_VENDOR_WEBGL, UNMASKED_RENDERER_WEBGL, every limit the
          client caches, the twelve shader precision formats, the line width
          and point size ranges, SUBPIXEL_BITS,
          MAX_TEXTURE_MAX_ANISOTROPY_EXT, MAX_DRAW_BUFFERS_WEBGL (WebGL1),
          and only the listed extensions. Values are set in the GPU process
          for WebGL contexts only, so Blink's own checks enforce the claim.
          Framebuffer-dependent values, context attributes, VERSION,
          SHADING_LANGUAGE_VERSION and readPixels stay live. A claim the host
          cannot back is logged.
Why:      Strings, extensions and limits must describe one GPU. A binding
          hook would leak through the client caches.
Profile:  gpu.webgl, gpu.webgl2: unmasked_vendor, unmasked_renderer,
          extensions, params, precision, max_anisotropy, max_draw_buffers
Hooks:    gpu/command_buffer/service/gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough.cc
          (GetCapabilities, GetGLCapabilities, PatchGetNumericResults);
          gles2_cmd_decoder_passthrough_doers.cc (DoGetString,
          DoGetShaderPrecisionFormat); new phasmid_webgl.{h,cc};
          third_party/blink/renderer/modules/webgl/
          webgl_rendering_context_base.cc (ExtensionSupportedAndAllowed)
Contexts: main, iframe, worker, shared worker, service worker, offscreen;
          WebGL1 and WebGL2
Guard:    tests/guards/graphics/webgl.py

